Q: Flextable horizontal align on Shiny page (the table, not the content) A: <p>I don't know how you define specify the table in the CSS file but I think that's the problem. I solved it with this code</p>
<pre><code>ui &lt;- fluidPage(
  shiny::tags$head(
    tags$style(
      &quot;.tabwid table {margin-left: 0px !important;}&quot;
    )
  ),

  fluidRow(
    uiOutput(&quot;flex&quot;)
  )
)
server &lt;- function(input, output) {

  output$flex &lt;- renderUI({
    tbl &lt;- head(mtcars)

    return(flextable(tbl) %&gt;%
      htmltools_value())        
  })
}
shinyApp(ui, server)
</code></pre>
<p>Please note the <code>.tabwid table</code> selector in the style tag I think this is the important step.</p>

Q: Prevent Firefox &#39;Save address?&#39; prompt on form submit in JavaScript address book app A: <h1>Workaround: Snapshot data, clear fields before send</h1>
<pre class="lang-js prettyprint-override"><code>function saveAddress() {
  const f=document.addContact;  //the original HTML form
  const fD = new FormData(f);   //copy the form data

  /* clear the address values in the HTML form */
  f.ax1.value=&quot;&quot;;f.ax2.value=&quot;&quot;;
  f.ax3.value=&quot;&quot;;f.ax4.value=&quot;&quot;;
  f.ax5.value=&quot;&quot;;f.ax6.value=&quot;&quot;;

  /* send the COPY of the form values to the server with fetch() */
  const pg=&quot;somepage.php&quot;;
  fetch(pg,{method:'post',credentials:'same-origin',body:fD})

  /*
    ... the rest of .then(function(response) {...} etc.
  */  
}
</code></pre>
<p>Firefox triggers the &quot;Save address?&quot; prompt on seeing address-pattern values in the DOM at/near submission time. By clearing them synchronously after capturing, the browser sees an &quot;empty&quot; form locally. This is the only solution I've found that reliably stops the annoying prompts without compromising accessibility or adding non-standard HTML. I've tested this on Firefox 143 and 147, and Chrome 144. If anyone has a cleaner way, please comment!</p>

Q: Avalonia DataGridCell not refreshed when using CellStyle A: <p>It has been solved by modifying the style like</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;Style Selector=&quot;DataGridCell.right-align &gt; TextBlock&quot;&gt;
    &lt;Setter Property=&quot;TextAlignment&quot; Value=&quot;Right&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Padding&quot; Value=&quot;0,0,4,0&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/Style&gt;
</code></pre>
<p>I've tried this before but the class name wasn't at the right place</p>
<pre class="lang-xml prettyprint-override"><code>&lt;Style Selector=&quot;DataGridCell &gt; TextBlock.right-align &quot;&gt;
    &lt;Setter Property=&quot;TextAlignment&quot; Value=&quot;Right&quot; /&gt;
    &lt;Setter Property=&quot;Padding&quot; Value=&quot;0,0,4,0&quot; /&gt;
&lt;/Style&gt;
</code></pre>
